    dipLede: 'Worried that “you raise cash, the Fed rescues the market and you miss the rebound”? Below is every time since 1976 the S&P 500 <b>first fell 15% below its high</b>. Most of the time it was higher 12 months later, but a few times (2001, 2008) it kept falling — and at the −15% moment the “rescue signals” (rate cuts, 2-year yield, credit spreads) could not tell which case it was.',
    watchH: 'Rescue watch (today’s readings, for observation only)',
